# Centralized Monitoring Station Configuration & Execution Log (192.168.1.30)

This document details the deployment, time-series telemetry configuration, and dashboard visualization gateway setup on the Monitoring Node.

---

## 1. Prometheus Setup & Time-Series Engine (Port 9090)
Downloaded, extracted, and configured Prometheus for pull-based metric scraping:
```bash
# Download and extract Prometheus binary package
wget https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/releases/download/v2.45.0/prometheus-2.45.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar -xvf prometheus-2.45.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
cd prometheus-2.45.0.linux-amd64

# Configure scraping targets and rules, then start Prometheus in the background
# Prometheus Configuration File (`prometheus.yml`)
Located at: `prometheus-2.45.0.linux-amd64/prometheus.yml`

vim promethus.yml
```yaml
# my global config
global:
  scrape_interval: 15s # Set the scrape interval to every 15 seconds. Default is every 1 minute.
  evaluation_interval: 15s # Evaluate rules every 15 seconds. The default is every 1 minute.

# Alertmanager configuration
alerting:
  alertmanagers:
    - static_configs:
        - targets:
          # - alertmanager:9093

# Load rules once and periodically evaluate them according to the global 'evaluation_interval'.
rule_files:
   - "alert_rules.yml"

# A scrape configuration containing endpoints to scrape:
scrape_configs:
  - job_name: "prometheus"
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["localhost:9090"]

  # --- PROJECT TARGET (SERVER 2) ---
  - job_name: "target-node"
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["192.168.1.20:9100"]

  - job_name: 'apache_status'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['192.168.1.20:9117']
!wq

[root@monitoring-server ~]# vim prometheus-2.45.0.linux-amd64/alert_rules.yml
groups:
  - name: server_health_alerts
    rules:
      # 1. Instance Down (Server status)
      - alert: InstanceDown
        expr: up == 0
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Server Offline!"
          description: "Target node is unreachable."

      # 2. Apache Service Alert (Web Server status)
      - alert: ApacheDown
        expr: apache_up == 0
        for: 30s
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Apache is DOWN!"
          description: "The Apache web server on the target node has stopped."

      # 3. High Memory Usage (> 90%)
      - alert: HighMemoryUsage
        expr: (node_memory_MemTotal_bytes - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes) / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes * 100 > 90
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High RAM Usage!"
          description: "Server RAM usage is above 90%."

      # 4. High CPU Load
      - alert: HighCPULoad
        expr: node_load1 > 1.5
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "High CPU Load!"
          description: "Target node CPU load is above 1.5."

./prometheus --config.file=prometheus.yml &

